<title>INDIA: Priority share allotment to small Indian investors.</title>
<headline>Priority share allotment to small Indian investors.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investors applying for up to 200 shares in a public issue will be given priority in allotment, Indian market watchdog Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>SEBI rules will be revised to ensure this, the market regulator said in a statement.</p>
<p>SEBI said mutual funds can advertise indicative returns for fixed income schemes to lure investors, but they must also state the risk factors as well.</p>
<p>--Bombay Newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
